{title: Shepherd of My Soul}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{key: F}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 81}

Verse 1
You are my [F]Shepherd.
I'll want for [Bm]nothing.
You make me [F]lie down
In pastures of [C]green.
Beside still [Dm]waters
And down paths of [Bm]righteousness
[Gm7]All for your [F]name's sake,
[C]Shepherd, you [F]lead.

Verse 2
You restore [Bm]my soul.  You restore [Dm7]my soul.
Surely goodness [F]and mercy will [Csus]follow.
[C]And I will [Dm]dwell in the house [Bm]of the Lord forever,
[F]There with my [C]Shepherd, [Bm]Shepherd [Gm7]of my [F]soul.

Verse 3
Even when [F]walking
Down through the [Bm]valley
There in [F]death's shadow
No evil I'll [C]fear.
You're always with [Dm]me.
Your rod and staff comfort [Bm]me.
[Gm7]Jesus, my [F]Shepherd,
[C]You're always [F]near.

Verse 4
You set a table before [Gm7]me,
With my [F/A]enemies all around.
[Dm]Let your anointing fall on [C]me.
Let my [F]cup overflow with your [Bm]pow'r.
